ter meter with mechanical indicating device, DN15\"\n  },\n  \"model_family\": {\n    \"family_name\": null,\n    \"models\": [\n      {\"model_id\": \"ET1\", \"label\": \"ET1, DN15\", \"attributes\": {}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"ET2\", \"label\": \"ET2, DN15\", \"attributes\": {}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"ET3\", \"label\": \"ET3, DN15\", \"attributes\": {}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"ET4\", \"label\": \"ET4, DN15\", \"attributes\": {}}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"characteristics\": {\n    \"type_level\": {\n      \"nominal_size_dn\": {\"value\": 15, \"unit_symbol\": \"mm\", \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []},\n      \"q2_over_q1_ratio\": {\"value\": 1.6, \"unit_symbol\": null, ...},\n      \"q4_over_q3_ratio\": {\"value\": 1.25, ...},\n      \"water_temperature_range\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 0.1, \"max\": 30}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"},\n      \"maximum_permitted_error_q2_to_q4\": {\"value\": 2, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"},\n      \"maximum_permitted_error_q1_to_q2\": {\"value\": 5, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"}\n    },\n    \"config_level\": [orientation entry, available classes entry]\n  },\n  \"matrix_tables\": [...7 tables...],\n  \"recommendation\": {\"id\": \"R49\", \"edition\": 2006, \"scheme\": \"B\"},\n  \"test_reports\": [{\"id\": \"PTB-1.5-4071210\", \"pages\": 2164, \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"}]\n}\n\nFor type_level values include footnote_markers: []? Schema shows footnote_markers as part of value object; include empty arrays or omit. I'll include only when present; but consistent shape: I'll include footnote_markers: [] — or omit for brevity. The strict shape requires value, unit_symbol, unit_id, footnote_markers. I'll include all keys for type_level. For nested values in model_level/config_level, keep {model/condition, value, unit_symbol}.\n\nFor the nominal_size: \"DN15\" — DN unitless effectively (DN 15 ≈ mm). unit_symbol \"mm\" is a reasonable interpretation. Or value \"DN15\" string. I'll do value 15, unit \"mm\".\n\nq4_over_q3_ratio: computed 1.25 —