ion\": \"ET2, Q3 = 1.6 m³/h, Q3/Q1 = 16–63\", \"value\": \"H\"}\n  ]\n}\n\nFor value strings here, value is a string \"H\" — allowed (string values OK).\n\nSecond config entry:\n{\n  \"attribute\": \"q3_over_q1_available_classes\",\n  \"axis\": \"model and Q3\",\n  \"values\": [\n    {\"condition\": \"ET1, ET3, ET4, Q3 = 2.5 m³/h, orientation H\", \"value\": {\"min\": 25, \"max\": 125}},\n    {\"condition\": \"ET1, ET3, ET4, Q3 = 2.5 m³/h, vertical\", \"value\": {\"min\": 25, \"max\": 50}},\n    {\"condition\": \"ET2, Q3 = 2.5 m³/h, orientation H\", \"value\": {\"min\": 25, \"max\": 100}},\n    {\"condition\": \"ET2, Q3 = 2.5 m³/h, vertical\", \"value\": {\"min\": 25, \"max\": 31.5}},\n    {\"condition\": \"ET1, ET3, ET4, Q3 = 1.6 m³/h, orientation H\", \"value\": {\"min\": 20, \"max\": 80}},\n    {\"condition\": \"ET1, ET3, ET4, Q3 = 1.6 m³/h, vertical\", \"value\": {\"min\": 20, \"max\": 31.5}},\n    {\"condition\": \"ET2, Q3 = 1.6 m³/h, orientation H\", \"value\": {\"min\": 16, \"max\": 63}}\n  ]\n}\n\nValues as {min,max} objects inside condition-values — value can be {min,max} per rule 2. OK.\n\nHmm — is this over-engineering? It's fine; conveys real info.\n\nAlso note: The two consecutive identical headings (\"ET1, ET3, ET4, DN15, Q₃ 2,5 m³/h\" twice) — second one is the vertical variant, as indicated by Orientation line. Good, handled.\n\nAlso note ET2 Q3=1.6 H — I only list one config (H). The trailing cut-off table presumably was vertical for ET2 Q3=1.6. Not present → omit.\n\nRecommendation: include amendment? none. \n\nAlso \"R 49-1/2/3\" parts — could include as separate? Schema has single id. Use \"R49\", edition 2006.\n\nLet me also double check decimal conversions: \"0,100\" → 0.1; \"0,079\" → 0.079; \"0,063\" → 0.063; \"0,050\" → 0.05; \"0,040\" → 0.04; \"0,031\" → 0.031; \"0,025\" → 0.025; \"0,020\" → 0.02; \"0,160\" → 0.16; \"0,127\"; \"0,100\" → 0.1; \"0,080\" → 0.08; \"0,063\" → 0.063; \"0,050\" → 0.05; \"0,040\" → 0.04; \"0,032\"; \"3,13\" → 3.13